        <div class="fc-delta-reason">IAEA inspectors have had no physical access to Iranian declared nuclear facilities since June 2025. Iran's stockpile stands at approximately 440.9 kg of 60%-enriched UF6 (unverified per IAEA as of last verified inspection). The June 17 MOU included a nuclear inspection clause within the 60-day negotiating period, but no IAEA access was confirmed before the MOU's contested expiry. Iran's FM Araghchi explicitly links IAEA access to US compliance with MOU provisions — specifically ending the naval blockade — a condition the US has not met. The 31-day window is short for bridging this gap, and the MOU ceasefire extension itself (F1) is uncertain as of Aug 14.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if the IAEA Director-General or Board of Governors officially confirms that inspectors physically entered and conducted verification activities at a named Iranian declared nuclear facility before EOD 2026-09-14. Remote monitoring (cameras or seals) without physical inspector presence = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IAEA official press releases or Board of Governors reports; or TIER1 quoting IAEA Director-General Grossi or Deputy DG for Safeguards by name with attribution on confirmed access.</dd>
