        <div class="fc-question">Will a TIER1-confirmed formal US-Iran negotiating session — with named delegation leads physically present or simultaneously on video conference — occur before EOD 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">45%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast · initial calibration 2026-08-14</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">The 74-day window is long enough to encompass at least one round of formal talks if the MOU extension holds. Iran's FM publicly denies direct negotiations with the US as of August 12–13, but the Pakistani and Omani intermediary channel is active with high-level engagement (Naqvi-Araghchi meeting Aug 13). Historical pattern: formal Islamabad sessions followed establishment of the intermediary channel within 60–90 days (February to April 2026 Islamabad Talks). Iran's preconditions (end US naval blockade, honor MOU) are demanding but not structurally impossible to partially meet given the Mecca Pact's new regional diplomacy context. Base rate: approximately one formal Pakistan-mediated session per 60–90 days since the April 2026 breakthrough.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
