  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Pakistani Interior Minister Naqvi arrived in Tehran on August 12–13 carrying a formal message from PM Sharif to Iranian FM Araghchi; multiple Pakistani government sources confirmed the meeting produced two hours of substantive exchange on MOU framework continuity. Iran's FM described the channel publicly as 'messages through intermediaries' in a state television statement on August 13, declining to characterize it as direct negotiations with the United States. No US government statement on the Naqvi-Araghchi meeting or its outcome had appeared by end of day August 14. → supports <span class="cite">F1</span></p>
      <p>Lloyd's List Intelligence recorded a single commercial transit through the Strait of Hormuz on August 9 — the lowest daily figure since the US naval blockade took full effect following the MOU's contested expiry in late July. The US Navy stopped and diverted a Panama-flagged general cargo vessel on August 11 that had attempted to breach the blockade, escorting it to a Pakistani port; no casualties were reported and Saudi Aramco confirmed the vessel's cargo as non-sanctioned goods. Iranian Deputy FM Gharibabadi told IRNA on August 5 that four Iran-Oman working groups on the Hormuz commercial framework had reached 'near-finalization' on three of four chapters; Oman's MOFA issued no parallel confirmation as of August 14. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span>, <span class="cite">F3</span></p>
      <p>The Houthi military spokesperson announced a named Saudi Arabia operations campaign on August 10; Houthi drone footage circulated on Yemen-monitored Telegram channels on August 9 allegedly from near the Jazan refinery, though Saudi Aramco and the Saudi government issued no confirmation of infrastructure damage or casualties. Saudi intelligence officials told Al Arabiya on August 6–7 that a coordinated Houthi-Iraqi PMF attack on Saudi civilian and energy sites was imminent. The Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, formally ratified at FM level on August 7 by Turkey, Saudi Arabia, and Pakistan, established a joint rapid-reaction force but includes no automatic trigger clause, and no member state had formally invoked it by August 14. → supports <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
      <p>August 9–11 polling by Haaretz placed the Eisenkot-led Yashar bloc at 60 seats collectively; Likud held 22–24 seats, with the Maariv poll of August 9 temporarily placing Likud at 24 — matching Eisenkot. An AFP-attributed Pentagon assessment of August 9 stated that IRGC command had ordered 'accelerated adversarial posture' options for a protracted-conflict scenario; the assessment was attributed to unnamed intelligence community sources. The USS George Washington carrier strike group entered the Arabian Sea on August 12 to replace the Eisenhower group on scheduled rotation. → supports <span class="cite">F7</span>, <span class="cite">F4</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

