      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (33%):</strong> Ceasefire extension fails or is not publicly confirmed (F1 NO, probability 0.45) and Houthi-PMF attack on Saudi Arabia meets the casualty or infrastructure threshold (F4 YES, probability 0.60) — joint probability ~33% when marginal widening risk included; triggering US-Iran direct military exchange or an expanded theater that forecloses the Pakistan-Oman diplomatic track for the remainder of 2026.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (55%):</strong> The dominant scenario — MOU extended short-term (F1 YES) but the Strait of Hormuz remains closed (F3 probability 0.18 against a 25-transit threshold from a baseline of 1 vessel per day), the Iran-Oman framework produces only a verbal announcement without a signed and released document (F2 NO), and no formal US-Iran session occurs through the Israeli election window (F6 NO) — the status quo of low-intensity naval standoff and Pakistani-mediated indirect channel persists into Q4 2026.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (12%):</strong> MOU extension confirmed (F1 YES, probability 0.55), Iran-Oman framework formally signed (F2 YES, probability 0.40), and Hormuz transits recover above 25 vessels per day (F3 YES) — joint probability approximately 12% when conditionalities between F1, F2, and F3 are applied; requires US partial blockade suspension and Iranian reciprocal compliance, a combination that current indicators make unlikely within 24 days.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media (IRNA, Tasnim) framed Naqvi's August 13 Tehran visit in terms of 'bilateral Iran-Pakistan strategic relations' in every headline, without naming the Islamabad ceasefire text or the MOU framework. Press TV's English service ran the meeting as 'diplomatic engagement for regional stability' with no reference to the United States. FM Araghchi delivered a formal on-camera statement to state television describing the channel as 'messages through intermediaries, not negotiations' — a formulation that IRNA and Tasnim have run consistently since June 14 across all coverage of the Pakistan track. → supports <span class="cite">F1</span></p>
      <p>IRIB's Friday sermon coverage of August 8 featured Khamenei's representative at Qom arguing that Iran's resistance economy had been validated by the Hormuz closure, and that any resumption of commercial transits required 'guarantees, not promises.' Kayhan ran three consecutive editorials August 10–12 characterizing the Pakistan channel as a face-saving mechanism for the United States rather than evidence of Iranian concession. Iran's Atomic Energy Organization head Eslami gave an IRNA interview on August 11 describing enrichment capacity as 'a scientific and sovereign achievement, independent of any diplomatic track.' → supports <span class="cite">F2</span></p>
      <p>Fars News ran two items August 11–12 on the Knesset election campaign, framing the Eisenkot bloc's polling lead as a product of Israeli war failure rather than domestic coalition dynamics. IRGC-affiliated Tasnim Telegram and Soroush platform compiled the Jazan drone footage on August 9–10 with commentary on Houthi operational capability; none of these items appeared on IRNA's official website in matching form, and no Iranian government official attributed the footage or endorsed the Houthi claim on record. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

