        <span class="p">5–10%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Khamenei, age 86, has not had a publicly confirmed health episode since June; IRGC command structure remains intact and has received expanded domestic authority under war-economy decrees. The Hormuz closure has consolidated nationalist sentiment around state-media framing of the conflict as a sovereignty defense rather than a crisis of governance. No credible internal succession contest observable in open sources; opposition networks inside Iran remain fragmented and without external logistics since the June crackdown. 12-month estimate unchanged from pre-gap baseline.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="regime-row">
        <span class="name">🇮🇱 Israel (Netanyahu Steps Down)</span>
        <span class="p">50–60%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Netanyahu has been caretaker PM since the Knesset completed its term and dissolved July 17 (62-0 self-directed vote). The October 27 election is 74 days away; current polling puts the Eisenkot-led bloc at 60 seats collectively, one short of a majority without Arab parties, while Likud holds 22–24 seats and trails Yashar individually. A Netanyahu electoral loss — roughly a 62% probability at current poll margins — would constitute stepping down within the 12-month window. Even a narrow Likud plurality leaves coalition formation deeply uncertain given Shas and UTJ positions on Haredi conscription. Range reflects this election-driven binary plus the residual possibility of health or legal developments.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
